{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008352-flexible-blood-feeding","id":1008352,"title":"Flexible Blood Feeding?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-25T18:06:00-08:00","id":1008352,"title":"Flexible Blood Feeding?","content":"To be honest, I never liked how in Requiem forces you to be required to feed on Vampire blood once their blood potency starts raising causing many restrictive gameplay, maybe is it possible to tweak and change some stuff to be more like Masquerade that the only that happens is if you started doing really bad stuff like mass dialabrie, mass embracing, mass blood bonding, etc all combined hence adopting &quot;Methuselah's Curse&quot;? I think it should be that no matter how high your blood potency is, Kindred should be able to feed on anything just like Generation from Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:27:21-08:00","id":1008358,"title":"","content":"The problem there is that in Masquerade elders are a rare elite whose numbers are more or less fixed. In Requiem blood potency 6+ just means that you're more than 250 years old. The feeding restrictions act as an incentive for vampires to go into torpor and let their blood potency fall. If it's not there there would be <i>way</i> too many powerful elders running around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:31:49-08:00","id":1008359,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there's Coils to circumvent all of this though? If that's the case then it would probably make the Ordo Dracul the most 'powerful' covenant around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:40:51-08:00","id":1008362,"title":"","content":"There was in first edition. Now Kindred can actually feed off anything as long as they spend a willpower per vitae if it's below their bp level, so it was a little redundant.<br /> <br /> There's also a scale of voivode where the dragon prepares a syringe with a cocktail of vitae and other crap and injects it into a human, and that makes the human's blood nourish anyone below blood potency 9 for a week.<br /> <br /> The other covenants have ways of getting around the restriction too, mind. The Invictus have Oaths, the Circle and the Lance have rituals, probably, the Carthians have... the short end of the stick, but they're mostly younger vampires anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-25-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:48:11-08:00","id":1008364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008352-flexible-blood-feeding?p=1008362#post1008362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also a scale of voivode where the dragon prepares a syringe with a cocktail of vitae and other crap and injects it into a human, and that makes the human's blood nourish anyone below blood potency 9 for a week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Up to and including 9, in fact. It lowers the effective blood potency of the vampire doing the drinking by 4 for the purposes of feeding restrictions, so BP 9 gets treated as 5, which is still able to feed on humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:12:18-08:00","id":1008372,"title":"","content":"Yeah, right, that's what I meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T09:21:00-08:00","id":1008945,"title":"","content":"There is that coil, but unnatural affinity also allows you to feed off werewolves, changelings, sin-eaters, beasts, ect ..<br /> <br /> So as far as tweaking.. There is already a system in place to allow you to not have to feed off vampires if you dont want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T10:21:40-08:00","id":1008962,"title":"","content":"If having your players worry about where their next meal is or should be coming from is not an issue you want to constantly go over, then ignore it. The restriction is just a glass ceiling to discourage players from making characters with high blood potency when starting out and meant to be easily ignored or bypassed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T10:24:57-08:00","id":1008964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008352-flexible-blood-feeding?p=1008962#post1008962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If having your players worry about where their next meal is or should be coming from is not an issue you want to constantly go over, then ignore it. The restriction is just a glass ceiling to discourage players from making characters with high blood potency when starting out and meant to be easily ignored or bypassed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, just remembered. even higher, you can spend a Willpower to feed 1 vitae off something you normally can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}